** CalculiX segmentation fault: an *EQUATION between the reference nodes of two rigid bodies
**
** Two bars of four C3D8 elements each, clamped at both far ends. One rigid body on the end face
** of each bar. A single equation ties the two reference nodes in the global x direction.
**
** ccx 2.21 and 2.22 crash without a message a second after "Nonlinear geometric effects are
** taken into account", writing no results. Deleting the three *Equation lines gives
** RigidBodyEquation_Solves.inp, which is the same model and solves.
